<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids slump as MGE falls.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids slump as MGE falls.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat cash bids were weaker on Friday, in line with lower MGE spring wheat futures, several cash grain dealers said.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures were down 7-3/4 cents per bushel for the December contract, the reference month used by most dealers to calculate flat prices.</p>
<p>Dealers noted weaker basis levels tied to harvest pressure in parts of North Dakota. Also, buyers were said to be scarce ahead of the three-day Labor Day weekend.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a holiday weekend so buyers are walking away from the market,&quot; a North Dakota dealer said.  </p>
